				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/madman-with-keyboard" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1616776); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1616776&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607526611" alt="Madman with Keyboard" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1616776)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/madman-with-keyboard" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1616776); return false;" >Madman with Keyboard</a></span> <span class="odate time_1509663588 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">02 Nov 2017 22:59</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-3625033">
									

<p>Well, it was certainly well written… Even if I have no clue who our main character was or what organization this was (UIU? That’s as best as I can guess), who those three people were or why they were targeted, what connection this had at all to that earlier mentioned burst of thaumaturgical energy, or why <strong><em>The Foundation</em></strong> of all people blew up a house with a Hellfire missile.</p>
<p>Like, the writing’s good and you have a nice prose going here, but the plot doesn’t really seem to have anything there, imho, and it’s such an abruot entry without cintext that I don’t really care for the character here.</p>
<p>If this is a companion piece or start up to something, then I’m interested, but as a stand alone, I’m just befuddled here.</p>

							</div>

								
					
