				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/afx-neuromancer" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2739221); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=2739221&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607526611" alt="AFX Neuromancer" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=2739221)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/afx-neuromancer" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2739221); return false;" >AFX Neuromancer</a></span> <span class="odate time_1510016234 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">07 Nov 2017 00:57</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-3627472">
									

<p>I admit the plot is fractured, and while I normally accept an ambiguous ending, this wouldn't satisfy me, either.</p>
<p>That being said, I figured if the response was positive (which it has been, so far&#8230;), I'd continue, and meant the ending to be a cliffhanger rather than a finale.</p>
<p>I'm not sure why you're confused why the three individuals were targeted; I thought that was one of the clearer aspects of the story. They were targeted because they triggered the Sothic spectrum analysis (assumed innocent until proven guilty, of course), and even a field agent like Nathan picked them out as the likely culprit. That's their connection. They <em>are</em> the connection to the thaumaturgical burst.</p>
<p>I'd like to say more is explained in the next part&#8230; but I've started writing it, and it picks up right where it left off with the explosion, with Nathan getting hit by the missile. I think there's so much action, there really isn't much room for explanation. I dunno&#8230;</p>
<p>Anyway guys&#8230; I just wanted to thank everyone for your comments. Don't wanna let you down.</p>

							</div>

								
